From c7509ca1fe8c40ae9808667f01540984ae13e1dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:37:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: ov13858: add the 4076x2806 mode used with the
 hardware ISP

The Windows driver reads a 4128x2848 window from (64,160) with ISP offsets
26/21 and outputs 4076x2806, with the same timing and PLL as 4224x3136
(30 fps). It is the only sensor mode in the Windows IPU7 graph settings
for this module, which the Surface Pro 12 uses with the IPU7 PSYS through
Intel's camera HAL. The Windows mode also sets both flips in 0x3820; here
they stay controls.

Register values are from the Windows ov13858.sys mode table (16-byte
entries {u32 1, u16 addr, u16 0, u32 val, u32 0}).

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov13858.c | 208 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 208 insertions(+)

